      <Docs>
        <param name="tids">The thread IDs to configure.</param>
        <summary>Sets the thread TIDs to track. The TIDs should belong to the same of the process that will make the headroom call. And they should not have different core affinity. If not set or set to empty, the headroom will be based on the PID of the process making the call. Parameters tids int : non-null list of TIDs, where maximum size can be read from SystemHealthManager.getMaxCpuHeadroomTidsSize() .</summary>
        <returns>The returned value is non-null.</returns>
